4. Never send signing secrets to the frontend.
5. Never place secrets in client-side environment variables.
6. Never print secrets in server logs.
7. Ensure previously issued tokens signed using the exposed secret are rejected.
8. Use a cryptographically secure token or session implementation.

### Recommended implementation

Prefer opaque random session tokens with server-side session validation and revocation.

If signed tokens are retained, use a well-established session library and proper key management.

Do not rely on the existing custom token implementation without addressing its security limitations.

